There is hereby established the Town of Tyrone Emergency Management Office. The mayor and council shall appoint a director of emergency management for the town. When appointed, the director will be a deputy director on the county emergency management staff and is charged:
(1) To represent the governing officials of the town on matters pertaining to emergency management;
(2) With assisting town officials in organizing town departments for emergency operations;
(3) With assisting in developing in conjunction with the county emergency management director, the plan for emergency functions for the county ordinance;
(4) With rendering reports such as required by governing officials; and
(5) With procuring, with authority of governing officials, a facility to be used as the town emergency operating center.
(Code 1984, § 3-3-2)

339:
In the event of an actual enemy attack upon the United States or any other disaster which may affect the lives and property of the citizens of the town, the mayor or, in his absence, his legally appointed successor may declare that a state of emergency exists and thereafter shall have and may exercise for such period as such state of emergency exists or continues the following emergency powers:
(1) To enforce all rules, laws, and regulations relating to emergency management and to assume direct operational control over all emergency management forces;
(2) To seize, take for temporary use, or condemn any property for the protection of the public;
(3) To sell, lend, give, or distribute all or any such property or supplies among the inhabitants of the town, to maintain a strict accounting of property or supplies distributed and for funds received for such property or supplies; and
(4) To perform and exercise such other functions and duties, and take such emergency actions as may be necessary to promote and secure the safety, protection and well being of the inhabitants of the town.
(Code 1984, § 3-3-3)

